WEBVTT

00:00:17.570 --> 00:00:18.700
Archer!

00:00:29.170 --> 00:00:31.670
All right, I'll be heading out with Sakura.

00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:35.090
When we're done shopping,
we'll be waiting at the park as usual.

00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:37.640
Let's meet up at 12 noon.

00:00:38.140 --> 00:00:39.390
Hold up, Rin.

00:00:39.680 --> 00:00:43.060
I know you two are off to enjoy your day off,

00:00:43.390 --> 00:00:46.020
but why bring me into it?

00:00:47.730 --> 00:00:50.150
We're talking about two girls going shopping.

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:53.400
Checking out lots of places. Don't you understand?

00:00:54.440 --> 00:00:56.280
Meaning you want me to carry your bags.

00:00:56.530 --> 00:00:58.030
We're so sorry!

00:00:59.990 --> 00:01:01.530
Understood.

00:01:01.990 --> 00:01:03.790
You go on and have a good time.

00:01:04.620 --> 00:01:05.710
Score!

00:01:06.410 --> 00:01:08.120
That's 12 o'clock at the park!

00:01:08.460 --> 00:01:10.210
Don't forget!

00:01:22.180 --> 00:01:24.810
I ended up arriving somewhat early.

00:01:25.480 --> 00:01:27.060
But that shouldn't matter.

00:01:27.600 --> 00:01:28.850
I'll just take it easy.

00:01:28.850 --> 00:01:30.560
Come on, let me go!

00:01:32.020 --> 00:01:33.820
I told you, I can't!

00:01:34.070 --> 00:01:36.320
Hey, don't be like that!

00:01:36.490 --> 00:01:37.860
It's just for a little while!

00:01:37.860 --> 00:01:39.780
But I've got stuff to do!

00:01:39.780 --> 00:01:41.160
Let go of me!

00:01:41.450 --> 00:01:43.080
Oh jeez!

00:01:44.080 --> 00:01:45.040
Hey!

00:01:45.700 --> 00:01:46.580
Darn.

00:01:46.830 --> 00:01:48.410
He got away.

00:01:59.050 --> 00:02:00.050
Hey.

00:02:02.050 --> 00:02:04.180
What do you want, Lancer?

00:02:04.810 --> 00:02:08.480
Well, you see, I have what you'd call a slight problem.

00:02:09.310 --> 00:02:10.520
Listen...

00:02:11.600 --> 00:02:14.020
You know how to cook, right?

00:02:16.990 --> 00:02:18.780
Welcome!

00:02:23.070 --> 00:02:24.830
Okay, please enjoy!

00:02:30.620 --> 00:02:32.290
Hey! I'll be right with you!

00:02:35.590 --> 00:02:37.590
How did I end up here?

00:02:38.630 --> 00:02:40.430
<i>Help me with my part-time job at the café!</i>

00:02:40.680 --> 00:02:41.720
<i>Declined.</i>

00:02:41.970 --> 00:02:44.050
<i>Man, you're so cold!</i>

00:02:44.300 --> 00:02:45.890
<i>Then I'll go ask the kid.</i>

00:02:46.140 --> 00:02:48.600
<i>Since he's probably the better cook.</i>

00:02:48.890 --> 00:02:49.810
<i>Hold on.</i>

00:02:51.060 --> 00:02:53.480
I let myself get competitive.

00:02:54.270 --> 00:02:55.400
Still...

00:03:00.650 --> 00:03:02.740
I suppose it's sufficiently equipped.

00:03:03.660 --> 00:03:06.200
Seriously, I owe you one!

00:03:06.410 --> 00:03:09.080
The chef bailed on short notice.

00:03:09.290 --> 00:03:12.620
And this place gets good reviews for its food,

00:03:12.870 --> 00:03:15.460
so it wasn't easy finding someone to fill in.

00:03:15.710 --> 00:03:17.670
I'm counting on you, Archer!

00:03:21.380 --> 00:03:22.880
<i>Eleven o'clock, huh?</i>

00:03:23.720 --> 00:03:27.560
<i>I'll need to go back when it's time to meet up.</i>

00:03:31.480 --> 00:03:32.890
Welcome!

00:03:35.730 --> 00:03:36.980
Oh no! What's this?

00:03:37.230 --> 00:03:40.490
Why do I see a familiar face before me?

00:03:40.740 --> 00:03:44.660
When all I wanted was to enjoy a
cup of tea with Master Souichirou!

00:03:44.660 --> 00:03:46.620
Go right ahead, then!

00:03:49.410 --> 00:03:52.080
I just can't relax.

00:03:56.040 --> 00:03:57.090
Caster.

00:03:57.340 --> 00:03:58.960
It doesn't matter where we are.

00:03:59.800 --> 00:04:03.630
The important thing is that we're together, am I right?

00:04:03.880 --> 00:04:06.720
M-Master Souichirou!

00:04:09.310 --> 00:04:11.180
Got an order for you!

00:04:11.470 --> 00:04:13.230
Two hot sandwiches.

00:04:13.730 --> 00:04:15.020
Roger that.

00:04:26.450 --> 00:04:27.700
Here they are.

00:04:31.910 --> 00:04:34.710
Keep up the good work, okay, Archer?

00:04:41.710 --> 00:04:44.420
I didn't know there was a café here.

00:04:45.180 --> 00:04:48.340
Come to think of it, it's lunchtime.

00:04:50.350 --> 00:04:52.140
Welcome!

00:04:56.270 --> 00:04:58.440
It's like you show up everywhere.

00:04:58.690 --> 00:05:00.190
You're working here, too?

00:05:00.520 --> 00:05:02.230
It's not just me, you know.

00:05:06.700 --> 00:05:08.910
Archer, what are you doing here?

00:05:09.160 --> 00:05:11.410
Don't make me explain it.

00:05:13.160 --> 00:05:14.750
I see that there's a lot going on here.

00:05:14.750 --> 00:05:16.580
Master Souichirou...

00:05:20.080 --> 00:05:21.420
What would you like?

00:05:29.340 --> 00:05:30.260
All right.

00:05:30.510 --> 00:05:33.100
I'll have the chef's suggestion, omurice!

00:05:34.220 --> 00:05:35.310
Gotcha!

00:05:36.350 --> 00:05:37.600
One omurice!

00:05:37.850 --> 00:05:39.350
You can handle that, right?

00:05:53.660 --> 00:05:54.910
Omurice.

00:05:56.540 --> 00:05:58.080
As you wish.

00:06:08.840 --> 00:06:10.470
Let's start with the sauce.

00:06:11.800 --> 00:06:16.350
Chop your garlic and saute it with olive oil.

00:06:17.350 --> 00:06:18.600
Add a can of tomatoes.

00:06:19.850 --> 00:06:21.480
And crushed consommé.

00:06:22.190 --> 00:06:23.150
Add salt,

00:06:23.730 --> 00:06:24.570
pepper,

00:06:25.110 --> 00:06:26.280
and sugar.

00:06:27.400 --> 00:06:29.450
Then melt some butter in it, and it's done.

00:06:39.580 --> 00:06:42.130
Next, coarsely chop an onion,

00:06:42.380 --> 00:06:44.170
and thinly slice some mushrooms.

00:06:44.840 --> 00:06:47.920
Then dice the chicken thighs.

00:06:49.050 --> 00:06:51.430
And these are your ingredients for the chicken rice.

00:06:55.890 --> 00:06:58.140
After you saute your chicken in a frying pan,

00:06:58.850 --> 00:07:03.560
add the onions and mushrooms, and saute some more.

00:07:04.360 --> 00:07:06.570
Next, add some salt, coarsely ground pepper,

00:07:06.980 --> 00:07:08.440
crushed consommé

00:07:09.030 --> 00:07:10.700
and ketchup.

00:07:11.610 --> 00:07:14.910
Mix it thoroughly to temper the sourness.

00:07:15.660 --> 00:07:17.160
Add your white rice.

00:07:18.120 --> 00:07:19.660
Fold it into the mixture.

00:07:20.250 --> 00:07:23.210
Then mix in the sauce, taking care not to let it burn.

00:07:30.630 --> 00:07:32.090
Welcome!

00:07:43.100 --> 00:07:44.650
The final part is the omelette itself.

00:07:44.900 --> 00:07:47.820
Heat some olive oil and butter in a frying pan.

00:07:48.110 --> 00:07:51.030
Add a dash of salt, then pour in a beaten egg.

00:07:52.110 --> 00:07:53.820
Mix it up with chopsticks.

00:07:54.740 --> 00:07:58.030
Shake the frying pan, and bring it to a half-cooked state.

00:07:58.580 --> 00:08:00.250
When it's half-cooked,

00:08:01.080 --> 00:08:03.250
slide it over to one side of the frying pan,

00:08:03.500 --> 00:08:05.120
adjust the shape,

00:08:05.380 --> 00:08:06.790
and flip it over.

00:08:07.500 --> 00:08:10.300
Keep flipping until the edge is on top.

00:08:12.470 --> 00:08:14.430
Then slide it onto the chicken rice.

00:08:20.390 --> 00:08:21.560
Done.

00:08:35.530 --> 00:08:37.620
A fluffy omurice.

00:08:38.990 --> 00:08:40.200
Now, then...

00:08:40.490 --> 00:08:41.740
Thank you for the meal.

00:08:53.260 --> 00:08:54.880
But this is delicious!

00:08:56.510 --> 00:08:58.600
Such a meticulous and delicate...

00:08:59.970 --> 00:09:01.220
And...

00:09:08.900 --> 00:09:10.520
...such a gentle taste.

00:09:12.360 --> 00:09:14.690
To think that you made this, Archer...

00:09:15.110 --> 00:09:17.910
So you do cook, too, after all.

00:09:20.490 --> 00:09:23.200
I'm glad you liked it.

00:09:27.210 --> 00:09:28.830
It's more than satisfying.

00:09:44.100 --> 00:09:45.980
The omurice was exquisite...

00:09:47.350 --> 00:09:48.310
Archer.

00:09:58.860 --> 00:10:00.110
Hey!

00:10:00.370 --> 00:10:01.870
Someone's asking for you!

00:10:02.370 --> 00:10:03.620
For me?

00:10:27.310 --> 00:10:28.770
This is on the house.

00:10:29.060 --> 00:10:30.270
Thanks.

00:10:36.110 --> 00:10:38.240
I guess you never noticed me.

00:10:38.860 --> 00:10:41.740
I borrowed these from Sakura to disguise myself.

00:10:42.160 --> 00:10:43.830
When I spotted you inside the café,

00:10:44.080 --> 00:10:47.580
I was intrigued, so I went inside to observe you.

00:10:48.540 --> 00:10:52.130
Sakura left, saying, "I'm good. I don't need to be here."

00:10:52.630 --> 00:10:55.500
But you were a sight to see in that kitchen!

00:10:57.300 --> 00:10:58.590
Sorry.

00:10:59.300 --> 00:11:01.220
I can't believe I did that.

00:11:02.050 --> 00:11:03.850
You mean not meeting up with us?

00:11:04.260 --> 00:11:05.760
I don't really mind.

00:11:06.560 --> 00:11:08.310
He filled me in on the situation.

00:11:08.560 --> 00:11:12.270
And in the first place,
I was the one who forced you into meeting us.

00:11:12.810 --> 00:11:14.270
Hey, so anyway,

00:11:14.520 --> 00:11:16.570
how did you like helping out at this café?

00:11:16.820 --> 00:11:18.900
Did you run into any trouble?

00:11:21.360 --> 00:11:24.160
What's wrong? Are you still feeling bad?

00:11:24.570 --> 00:11:25.530
Then,

00:11:25.830 --> 00:11:27.040
omurice!

00:11:27.540 --> 00:11:31.040
What Saber just had. Make it for me sometime!

00:11:31.580 --> 00:11:33.120
Then we'll call it even!

00:11:36.710 --> 00:11:37.800
Okay.

00:11:39.590 --> 00:11:41.260
I'll make as many as you want.

00:12:02.950 --> 00:12:04.070
Shirou! Shirou!

00:12:04.450 --> 00:12:05.700
Listen to me!

00:12:06.370 --> 00:12:09.990
Today, I partook of Archer's cooking at the café!

00:12:13.410 --> 00:12:15.210
Was it good?

00:12:16.130 --> 00:12:18.710
Yes, it was quite exquisite!

00:12:19.880 --> 00:12:21.090
I see.

00:12:22.170 --> 00:12:25.970
All right, Saber, I'm adding two
more dishes to tonight's meal!

00:12:26.260 --> 00:12:28.100
I'm pulling out all the stops!

00:12:30.220 --> 00:12:30.970
Shirou?
